extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_JOE_RESEARCH_FILES: G.I. JOE RESEARCH
    STR_STANDARD_ISSUE: Standard Issue
    STR_STANDARD_ISSUE_UFOPEDIA: The rifles, pistols and submachine guns the Joes carry on Day 1, and the signature weapons each named Joe brings with him.
    STR_STANDARD_EXPLOSIVES: Standard Explosives
    STR_STANDARD_EXPLOSIVES_UFOPEDIA: 'Fragmentation and smoke grenades: Army issue, bought and delivered.'
    STR_STANDARD_FATIGUES: Standard Fatigues
    STR_STANDARD_FATIGUES_UFOPEDIA: Every Joe's own uniform, and flak vests for the greenshirts.
    STR_FIELD_MEDICINE: Field Medicine
    STR_FIELD_MEDICINE_UFOPEDIA: Medkits and the training to use them under fire.
    STR_BREACHING_SHOTGUN: Breaching Shotgun
    STR_BREACHING_SHOTGUN_UFOPEDIA: Pump shotguns for close quarters and for doors that will not open.
    STR_KEVLAR_VEST: Kevlar Vest
    STR_KEVLAR_VEST_UFOPEDIA: Soft body armour that stops pistol rounds and fragments. Heavier than a flak vest and worth it.
    STR_AP_ROUNDS: Armor-Piercing Rounds
    STR_AP_ROUNDS_UFOPEDIA: Hardened-core magazines for the rifles, the sniper rifle and Roadblock's .50 cal. For targets behind steel.
    STR_FIELD_RADIO: Field Radio
    STR_FIELD_RADIO_UFOPEDIA: A man-pack radio like Breaker's. A Joe carrying one can call in support the base has researched.
    STR_NIGHT_VISION: Night-Vision Goggles
    STR_NIGHT_VISION_UFOPEDIA: Starlight goggles. Joes wearing them see as far at night as Cobra does in the day.
    STR_VAMP: VAMP
    STR_VAMP_UFOPEDIA: 'The Multi-Purpose Attack Vehicle: a fast four-wheel-drive with a twin machine gun. Two Joes, any road.'
    STR_SKYSTRIKER: Skystriker
    STR_SKYSTRIKER_UFOPEDIA: 'The Skystriker XP-14F: G.I. Joe''s swing-wing fighter. It needs a hangar. Upgrades keep it Joe''s dogfighter for the whole war.'
    STR_RADAR_ROOM: Radar Room
    STR_RADAR_ROOM_UFOPEDIA: A radar room for The Pit. Until it is built, Cobra is found only through leads, intel and its own mistakes.
    STR_C130_HERCULES: C-130 Hercules
    STR_C130_HERCULES_UFOPEDIA: Strategic airlift. The A.P.C. cannot cross water; the Hercules can carry a squad and its vehicles to another continent, if there is a landing zone at the other end.
    STR_PENTAGON_BUDGET_REVIEW: Pentagon Budget Review
    STR_PENTAGON_BUDGET_REVIEW_UFOPEDIA: Three months in, the Pentagon has reviewed G.I. Joe and released the rest of the equipment budget. More hardware can now be researched.
    STR_MATCH_GRADE_OPTICS: Match-Grade Optics
    STR_MATCH_GRADE_OPTICS_UFOPEDIA: 'Scopes for the M-16: a marksman in every squad.'
    STR_C4_DEMOLITIONS: C-4 Demolitions
    STR_C4_DEMOLITIONS_UFOPEDIA: Satchel charges that open walls and doors.
    STR_CLAYMORE_MINES: Claymore Mines
    STR_CLAYMORE_MINES_UFOPEDIA: Directional mines for ambushes and for guarding a flank.
    STR_MOBAT: MOBAT
    STR_MOBAT_UFOPEDIA: 'The Motorized Battle Tank: G.I. Joe''s first tank.'
    STR_RAM: R.A.M.
    STR_RAM_UFOPEDIA: 'The Rapid-fire Motorcycle: a scout bike with a machine gun in a sidecar.'
    STR_HAL: H.A.L.
    STR_HAL_UFOPEDIA: 'The Heavy Artillery Laser: a towed laser cannon.'
    STR_FLAK: F.L.A.K.
    STR_FLAK_UFOPEDIA: A towed anti-aircraft gun for The Pit and the outposts.
    STR_WOLVERINE: Wolverine
    STR_WOLVERINE_UFOPEDIA: 'An armoured missile carrier: light tank and fire support.'
    STR_SLUGGER: Slugger
    STR_SLUGGER_UFOPEDIA: 'A self-propelled cannon: artillery on the battle map.'
    STR_POLAR_BATTLE_BEAR: Polar Battle Bear
    STR_POLAR_BATTLE_BEAR_UFOPEDIA: A tracked arctic vehicle, at its best in snow and ice.
    STR_MMS: M.M.S.
    STR_MMS_UFOPEDIA: 'The Mobile Missile System: off-map missile support a Joe with a radio can call in.'
    STR_MOUNTAIN_HOWITZER: Mountain Howitzer
    STR_MOUNTAIN_HOWITZER_UFOPEDIA: A light howitzer for off-map fire support.
    STR_DRAGONFLY: Dragonfly
    STR_DRAGONFLY_UFOPEDIA: An attack helicopter that flies over the battle map.
    STR_FALCON_GLIDER: Falcon Glider
    STR_FALCON_GLIDER_UFOPEDIA: A silent glider for night insertions.
    STR_SKY_HAWK: Sky Hawk
    STR_SKY_HAWK_UFOPEDIA: A light VTOL that escorts transports.
    STR_SHARC: S.H.A.R.C.
    STR_SHARC_UFOPEDIA: 'A flying submarine: air and underwater.'
    STR_MANTA: MANTA
    STR_MANTA_UFOPEDIA: A small amphibious assault craft.
    STR_KILLER_WHALE: Killer W.H.A.L.E.
    STR_KILLER_WHALE_UFOPEDIA: A hovercraft assault transport for squads and light vehicles.
    STR_JUMP_JET_PACK: J.U.M.P. Jet Pack
    STR_JUMP_JET_PACK_UFOPEDIA: A jet pack launched from a ground platform.
    STR_PAC_RATS: PAC/RATs
    STR_PAC_RATS_UFOPEDIA: 'Remote-controlled tracked weapons: machine gun, flamethrower and missile.'
    STR_BATTLE_STATIONS: Battle Stations
    STR_BATTLE_STATIONS_UFOPEDIA: Machine gun, missile and mortar defense units for The Pit and the outposts.
    STR_WATCH_TOWER: Watch Tower
    STR_WATCH_TOWER_UFOPEDIA: A tower that spots Cobra sooner, and makes the base easier to spot.
    STR_BIVOUAC: Bivouac
    STR_BIVOUAC_UFOPEDIA: 'A field camp: cheap barracks for outposts.'
    STR_SQUAD_AUTOMATIC_WEAPON: Squad Automatic Weapon
    STR_SQUAD_AUTOMATIC_WEAPON_UFOPEDIA: 'The M249 SAW: a light machine gun for the squad.'
    STR_INCENDIARY_ROUNDS: Incendiary Rounds
    STR_INCENDIARY_ROUNDS_UFOPEDIA: Incendiary ammunition for the .50 cal and the grenade launcher.
    STR_CONCUSSION_GRENADE: Concussion Grenade
    STR_CONCUSSION_GRENADE_UFOPEDIA: A stun grenade. Prisoners feed the trail; this takes them alive.
    STR_THERMITE: Thermite
    STR_THERMITE_UFOPEDIA: Thermite grenades that burn through doors and vehicles.
    STR_LASER_GUIDED_ROCKETS: Laser-Guided Rockets
    STR_LASER_GUIDED_ROCKETS_UFOPEDIA: A guided round for the rocket launcher.
    STR_JOE_COBRA_GRENADE: Joe-Built Cobra Grenade
    STR_JOE_COBRA_GRENADE_UFOPEDIA: Cobra's own grenade design, built in our shop.
    STR_GHILLIE_SUIT: Ghillie Suit
    STR_GHILLIE_SUIT_UFOPEDIA: Sniper camouflage.
    STR_ARCTIC_GEAR: Arctic Gear
    STR_ARCTIC_GEAR_UFOPEDIA: Cold-weather suits for polar missions.
    STR_NINJA_GEAR: Ninja Gear
    STR_NINJA_GEAR_UFOPEDIA: 'What the Arashikage prisoner wore and how it is made: a stealth suit in the Snake Eyes style.'
    STR_COMBAT_STIMS: Combat Stims
    STR_COMBAT_STIMS_UFOPEDIA: A stim pack that restores energy and cuts stun.
    STR_TRAUMA_KIT: Trauma Kit
    STR_TRAUMA_KIT_UFOPEDIA: 'Built from the Medi-Viper''s kit: a trauma kit that heals more than a medkit.'
    STR_INFIRMARY: Infirmary
    STR_INFIRMARY_UFOPEDIA: 'An infirmary for The Pit: wounded Joes recover faster.'
    STR_VAMP_MK2: VAMP Mk II
    STR_VAMP_MK2_UFOPEDIA: The VAMP with a heavier gun and more armour.
    STR_TWIN_BATTLE_GUN: Twin Battle Gun
    STR_TWIN_BATTLE_GUN_UFOPEDIA: A twin anti-aircraft gun.
    STR_ANTI_AIRCRAFT_GUN: Anti-Aircraft Gun
    STR_ANTI_AIRCRAFT_GUN_UFOPEDIA: A heavy anti-aircraft gun emplacement.
    STR_SNOW_CAT: Snow Cat
    STR_SNOW_CAT_UFOPEDIA: A big arctic half-track with missiles. Frostbite comes with it.
    STR_DEVILFISH: Devilfish
    STR_DEVILFISH_UFOPEDIA: A fast attack boat.
    STR_SONAR_SUITE: Sonar Suite
    STR_SONAR_SUITE_UFOPEDIA: Sonar that finds submarines and divers.
    STR_STOP_AND_SEARCH: Stop and Search Teams
    STR_STOP_AND_SEARCH_UFOPEDIA: Boarding a ship without a fight, and without sinking an innocent merchant.
    STR_AVALANCHE_MISSILE: Avalanche Missile
    STR_AVALANCHE_MISSILE_UFOPEDIA: A heavy air-to-air missile, good against bombers.
    STR_TOMAHAWK: Tomahawk
    STR_TOMAHAWK_UFOPEDIA: 'A twin-rotor helicopter transport: hot landing zones, not just airfields.'
    STR_MUDFIGHTER: Mudfighter
    STR_MUDFIGHTER_UFOPEDIA: A strike plane for close air support.
    STR_SKYSTRIKER_MK2: Skystriker Mk II
    STR_SKYSTRIKER_MK2_UFOPEDIA: Better radar and a tighter turn, from what the Rattler wreck taught us.
    STR_AIR_COMBAT_DOCTRINE: Air Combat Doctrine
    STR_AIR_COMBAT_DOCTRINE_UFOPEDIA: How Cobra's pilots are taught to fly, and how to beat them. Every Joe aircraft is more accurate.
    STR_DETENTION_BLOCK: Detention Block
    STR_DETENTION_BLOCK_UFOPEDIA: Cells for Cobra prisoners, with room to grow. The trail runs through the men we take alive.
    STR_SIGNALS_INTELLIGENCE_CENTER: Signals Intelligence Center
    STR_SIGNALS_INTELLIGENCE_CENTER_UFOPEDIA: A listening post in The Pit. Cobra's radio traffic becomes leads.
    STR_LONG_RANGE_RADAR: Long-Range Radar
    STR_LONG_RANGE_RADAR_UFOPEDIA: A radar with a far longer reach.
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
